WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.700 --> 00:00:05.370
It goes without saying that Ace and his role
in the story of One Piece, have been a wildly

00:00:05.370 --> 00:00:07.439
controversial topic.

00:00:07.439 --> 00:00:12.349
Many adore his character for its cool and
charming design, while many others criticise

00:00:12.349 --> 00:00:15.639
it for its lack of character development and
impulsive behaviour.

00:00:15.639 --> 00:00:21.540
And at the height of this debate stands of
course the CLIMAX of Ace´s tragic story arc:

00:00:21.540 --> 00:00:27.790
his defeat by Blackbeard, his capture by the
Marines, his liberation by Luffy and finally,

00:00:27.790 --> 00:00:30.180
his sacrifice for his younger brother.

00:00:30.180 --> 00:00:35.730
A common point of criticism regarding Ace´s
death, is that Ace did not have enough character

00:00:35.730 --> 00:00:39.870
development to make his death feel impactful
enough.

00:00:39.870 --> 00:00:45.100
And while emotional connection to a character
is, and always WILL be, a subjective experience

00:00:45.100 --> 00:00:51.010
for EVERY one of us, I find that this argument
is somewhat missing the point of Ace´s role

00:00:51.010 --> 00:00:52.890
in the story.

00:00:52.890 --> 00:00:58.440
Because not every character in a story can,
or even SHOULD undergo character development.

00:00:58.440 --> 00:01:03.320
In fact there are three types of character
arcs that a character can go through: Positive

00:01:03.320 --> 00:01:07.689
change, negative change or, no change at all.

00:01:07.689 --> 00:01:13.719
Ace, just as many other important side characters
in the story, has a FLAT character arc; meaning

00:01:13.719 --> 00:01:18.219
he doesn’t change his view on the world,
but stays a constant throughout his appearances

00:01:18.219 --> 00:01:20.090
in the story.

00:01:20.090 --> 00:01:25.280
His entire life, Ace is struggling with the
legacy of his fathers name, having to suffer

00:01:25.280 --> 00:01:31.189
under both the burning hatred as well as the
flaming admiration people had for Roger.

00:01:31.189 --> 00:01:37.030
Being born as the son of the WORST criminal
of his age, until his very last moment, Ace

00:01:37.030 --> 00:01:41.539
is struggling to find meaning in his life
and whether he ever deserved to live in the

00:01:41.539 --> 00:01:43.170
first place.

00:01:43.170 --> 00:01:48.240
The ONE thing he can cling on to is his burning
will to protect his friends and family from

00:01:48.240 --> 00:01:49.240
any harm.

00:01:49.240 --> 00:01:54.060
His death therefore, was one of the most SHOCKING
events in the entirety of One Piece.

00:01:54.060 --> 00:02:00.529
Especially so, since Oda is very careful and
averse when it comes to killing off characters.

00:02:00.529 --> 00:02:05.749
And most importantly, Ace´s death was not
a Disney death, where the person comes back

00:02:05.749 --> 00:02:07.079
to life in the end.

00:02:07.079 --> 00:02:15.360
No, what makes this moment so INCREDIBLY powerful
is that it is FINAL, and has real consequences.

00:02:15.360 --> 00:02:20.700
And therefore, in this video, I want to talk
about the tragedy of Portages D. Ace, and

00:02:20.700 --> 00:02:26.189
why his death is one of THE fundamental cornerstones
of the One Piece story.

00:02:26.189 --> 00:02:31.900
Because Luffy loosing his beloved older brother
not only deepens our protagonist´s character,

00:02:31.900 --> 00:02:41.000
but it ALSO advances the plot in a crucial
way, and of course also impacts US, the readers,

00:02:41.000 --> 00:02:45.030
emotionally.

00:02:45.030 --> 00:02:49.719
When I talk about how Ace´s death has deepened
Luffy´s character, I believe it goes MUCH

00:02:49.719 --> 00:02:53.200
deeper than simply showing Luffy that he has
to become stronger.

00:02:53.200 --> 00:02:58.709
In fact, Luffy already was aware of this back
on Water 7, when he talks to Bruno about his

00:02:58.709 --> 00:03:01.189
devastating defeat by Aokiji.

00:03:01.189 --> 00:03:06.090
And of course, loosing his crew to Kizaru
and Kuma, against both of whom he stood not

00:03:06.090 --> 00:03:12.049
the slightest chance, also made Luffy realise
that he had to become much more powerful.

00:03:12.049 --> 00:03:17.220
So no; Ace´s death was NOT simply a way for
Luffy to become stronger.

00:03:17.220 --> 00:03:21.170
Loosing his treasured older brother, whom
he had shared such a happy and adventurous

00:03:21.170 --> 00:03:27.700
childhood with, shook Luffy to his core and
from there developed his character fundamentally.

00:03:27.700 --> 00:03:32.189
Having the loving bond with his brother cut,
JUST when he had managed to finally do the

00:03:32.189 --> 00:03:38.349
impossible and save him from the marines,
threw Luffy into deep distress and despair.

00:03:38.349 --> 00:03:43.879
Being characterised by his positive, easy-going
and at times naive nature, Luffy has to learn

00:03:43.879 --> 00:03:48.540
that not every obstacle can be overcome through
determination alone.

00:03:48.540 --> 00:03:53.499
For the FIRST time EVER, he was not able to
fulfil a goal he set himself.

00:03:53.499 --> 00:03:58.290
He gave EVERYTHING he had to save his brother,
and still he failed.

00:03:58.290 --> 00:04:03.310
He realises that loss and failure are things
that can actually happen to him if he is not

00:04:03.310 --> 00:04:05.569
willing to take things seriously.

00:04:05.569 --> 00:04:08.269
But it goes even further than this.

00:04:08.269 --> 00:04:12.629
It makes Luffy question his entire purpose
for setting out to sea.

00:04:12.629 --> 00:04:17.570
Loosing BOTH, his crew AND Ace, it is an absolute
low point in his adventure.

00:04:17.570 --> 00:04:23.300
However, the experience allows him to realise
that his crew are not only his friends, but

00:04:23.300 --> 00:04:28.890
his FAMILY, and that he has to grow significantly
in order to be able to protect them from Ace´s

00:04:28.890 --> 00:04:29.890
fate.

00:04:29.890 --> 00:04:35.750
Thus, he literally inherits Ace´s will to
protect those he holds dear at any cost.

00:04:35.750 --> 00:04:41.470
It is the decicive trigger for Luffy, to become
the powerful and more mature captain he is

00:04:41.470 --> 00:04:42.470
today.

00:04:42.470 --> 00:04:47.440
And finally, seeing his brother murdered in
front of his eyes also gave Luffy his first

00:04:47.440 --> 00:04:51.500
ever antagonist, that he resents on a PERSONAL
level.

00:04:51.500 --> 00:04:56.760
Killing Ace and literally BURNING the mark
of his death into Luffy´s chest, is a permanent

00:04:56.760 --> 00:05:00.880
visual reminder of what the Admiral did to
our protagonist.

00:05:00.880 --> 00:05:06.560
In the end, Luffy comes out of his grieve
as a stronger, wiser and overall more mature

00:05:06.560 --> 00:05:12.880
captain, facing a strong antagonist that he
truly resents with ALL his heart.

00:05:12.880 --> 00:05:21.350
But Ace´s tragic character arc does even
MORE for the story than developing Luffy.

00:05:21.350 --> 00:05:26.200
It advances the plot line SIGNIFICANTLY and
sets the stage for the second half of the

00:05:26.200 --> 00:05:27.470
story.

00:05:27.470 --> 00:05:31.580
While some people disliked Ace´s defeat by
Blackbeard and his subsequent capture by the

00:05:31.580 --> 00:05:36.470
world government, these events not only introduced
Blackbeard as Luffy´s biggest rival for the

00:05:36.470 --> 00:05:42.290
story, but it placed Luffy, as Ace´s little
brother, right at the CENTER of the Impel

00:05:42.290 --> 00:05:44.890
Down and Marineford arcs.

00:05:44.890 --> 00:05:50.710
This was crucial, since both arcs did not
only introduce a ton of important new characters,

00:05:50.710 --> 00:05:56.990
but also rang in the end of Roger´s and Whitebeard´s
era and the beginning of a new age.

00:05:56.990 --> 00:06:01.460
Since ACE wanted to make WHITEBEARD King of
the pirates, and WHITEBEARD in turn to make

00:06:01.460 --> 00:06:06.590
ACE pirate King, there was little room for
Luffy to come closer to his goal.

00:06:06.590 --> 00:06:12.840
The new power vacuum created by Whitebeard´s
death was not only convenient, but NECESSARY

00:06:12.840 --> 00:06:19.200
for BOTH Luffy AND Blackbeard to have a realistic
shot at finding the One Piece.

00:06:19.200 --> 00:06:25.270
And this war taking place and Luffy being
able to be present there, was only possible,

00:06:25.270 --> 00:06:30.740
because his adopted brother, the son of the
former pirate King himself, was to be publicly

00:06:30.740 --> 00:06:33.550
executed and politicised by the world government.

00:06:33.550 --> 00:06:40.030
And beside that, the war AND Luffy´s tragic
loss also served as a midpoint climax to the

00:06:40.030 --> 00:06:44.820
entire series, which gave the adventure a
fresh start after the time skip and better

00:06:44.820 --> 00:06:46.240
pacing overall.

00:06:46.240 --> 00:06:51.110
In this context it also allowed us to see
Luffy reflect upon his childhood with Ace

00:06:51.110 --> 00:06:57.460
and Sabo, and thus gave us a much deeper look
into the development and history of his character.

00:06:57.460 --> 00:07:03.040
So to put it shortly: Ace´s character was
designed to enable CRUCIAL plot development

00:07:03.040 --> 00:07:08.850
for the one piece story that resulted in one
of the most POPULAR arcs of the series AND

00:07:08.850 --> 00:07:15.800
set the stage for the second half of the adventure
in the new world.

00:07:15.800 --> 00:07:22.730
Now, It would be quite heartless of me of
course, to say that Ace´s character was simply

00:07:22.730 --> 00:07:27.200
an elegant tool, smartly fit into the story
to develop Luffy and the plot.

00:07:27.200 --> 00:07:32.930
Because, as I said in the beginning, for many,
Ace was a DEEPLY likeable character.

00:07:32.930 --> 00:07:38.650
Thus, his death obviously had a strong emotional
impact on us readers as well.

00:07:38.650 --> 00:07:44.810
However, even if you did not like or care
for Ace TOO much before his execution, I think

00:07:44.810 --> 00:07:50.340
that the moment he died was nonetheless powerful
for pretty much any reader.

00:07:50.340 --> 00:07:55.020
Because not only did Ace sacrifice his just
regained life for his little brother Luffy,

00:07:55.020 --> 00:08:00.370
but Oda also found a quite emotional, and
yet weirdly satisfying end to his character

00:08:00.370 --> 00:08:01.370
arc.

00:08:01.370 --> 00:08:07.270
Firstly, the true MAGNITUDE of a minor characters
death is ALWAYS defined by the reaction of

00:08:07.270 --> 00:08:09.910
the hero, who we all emphasise with.

00:08:09.910 --> 00:08:15.250
And Luffy´s reaction to Ace´s death might
very well be the most POWERFUL and HEARTBREAKING

00:08:15.250 --> 00:08:19.380
thing we have had to witness in the entire
series so far.

00:08:19.380 --> 00:08:24.870
This fact alone gave this moment, and thus
Ace´s character, a lot of meaning; actually

00:08:24.870 --> 00:08:28.410
making him even MORE popular after his death.

00:08:28.410 --> 00:08:33.140
And secondly, Ace finally managed to find
an answer to the question that has haunted

00:08:33.140 --> 00:08:37.220
him his entire life: Why do I live?

00:08:37.220 --> 00:08:41.780
All his life Ace was known for never turning
his back on an enemy, no matter HOW strong

00:08:41.780 --> 00:08:42.940
they were.

00:08:42.940 --> 00:08:47.320
And when he finally accepts WHITEBEARD and
his men as his new family, he proudly wears

00:08:47.320 --> 00:08:49.990
his mark on his back, where it could never
be harmed.

00:08:49.990 --> 00:08:50.990
Because Ace was known for never turning his
back on an enemy.

00:08:50.990 --> 00:08:57.030
And yet, DESPITE his pride, the LAST thing
he does is turning his back on Akainu in order

00:08:57.030 --> 00:08:58.990
to protect his family.

00:08:58.990 --> 00:09:04.230
Having Luffy and Whitebeard taking on the
world government for his sake shows him that

00:09:04.230 --> 00:09:07.710
people actually do care whether he lives or
not.

00:09:07.710 --> 00:09:10.340
He actually deserves to live.

00:09:10.340 --> 00:09:16.830
And so just having found his answer, he chooses
to protect his family over all else.

00:09:16.830 --> 00:09:20.370
And this will, he then inherits to Luffy.

00:09:20.370 --> 00:09:25.510
What we can take away from all this, is that
Ace´s character is much more than a cool

00:09:25.510 --> 00:09:31.130
older brother who’s death motivated Luffy
to train for two years and get stronger.

00:09:31.130 --> 00:09:35.570
The hardship and doubt that he carried in
his heart his entire life, as well as the

00:09:35.570 --> 00:09:41.480
love he felt for his family, lead to the most
IMPACTFUL event in the story up to this point.

00:09:41.480 --> 00:09:46.530
Not only did he give significant character
development to Luffy, but he also shaped and

00:09:46.530 --> 00:09:50.380
developed the plot of the story in a number
of crucial ways.

00:09:50.380 --> 00:09:55.700
And in the end, his death drove home one of
the most, if not THE most, important theme

00:09:55.700 --> 00:09:58.760
in One Piece: Following your dreams.

00:09:58.760 --> 00:10:04.280
Because, with Ace dying in the end with a
smile on his face, just as his father did,

00:10:04.280 --> 00:10:09.610
Oda tells us that if you pursue your dream
and strive for what you really wanted in life,

00:10:09.610 --> 00:10:18.560
you will have a happy ending.

00:10:18.560 --> 00:10:21.000
Hey everyone, thank you so much for watching.

00:10:21.000 --> 00:10:23.330
